---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL || '/';
const withBase = (path: string) => base === '/' ? path : base.replace(/\/$/, '') + path;
const deckPath = withBase('/New%20CS%204775%20Presentation%20Draft%20(3).pdf');
---

<BaseLayout title="Benchmark Lineage Visualizer" sideBarActiveItemID="projects">
  <article class="prose max-w-none">
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center gap-4 mb-6">
      <img src={withBase('/logos/cornell-logo.png')} alt="Cornell logo" class="max-h-14 md:max-h-16" loading="lazy" />
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold leading-tight">Benchmark Lineage Visualizer</h1>
    </div>

    <p class="text-base leading-relaxed">
      I designed a lightweight visualization to trace benchmark lineage across experiments for my Cornell course project.
      I implemented each benchmark algorithm in the deck and ran them on both a synthetic dataset (to isolate edge cases) and
      a real dataset (to validate practical gains), so we could compare how configuration drift impacted results. The PDF deck
      below captures the runs, lineage views, and takeaways for our team retro.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What I shipped</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc ml-6 space-y-2">
        <li>Mapped experiment metadata into a lineage graph to show parent/child benchmarks and configuration drift.</li>
        <li>Added quick filters for dataset, model family, and run date to spot anomalies and regression points.</li>
        <li>Implemented and benchmarked the listed algorithms on synthetic and real datasets, then summarized findings in a slide deck for team retro.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Execution & report plan (team)</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc ml-6 space-y-2">
        <li>Run SCITE, SiFit, PhISCS-BnB, and Neighbor-Joining on the real single-cell tumor dataset with consistent preprocessing and logged parameters.</li>
        <li>Compare real-data lineage trees to synthetic patterns (balanced/comb/mixed) for depth, branching, noise sensitivity, and clade stability.</li>
        <li>Collect numeric comparators: pairwise tree distances where applicable, depth/internal node counts, runtime/cost for each method.</li>
        <li>Divide writing: Methods (Ena), computational cost (Claire), biological interpretation (Alex), real-data execution/analysis (Jake & Sophia), integration/review (Alyssa).</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Slides</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 flex gap-3 flex-wrap">
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" href={deckPath} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Open slides in new tab
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" href={deckPath} download>
          Download (PDF)
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-4 bg-base-200/60 border rounded-lg shadow overflow-hidden">
        <object
          data={deckPath}
          type="application/pdf"
          class="w-full h-[80vh]">
          <div class="p-3 text-center text-sm">
            <p class="mb-2">If the embedded PDF doesn’t load, use the buttons above to open or download.</p>
            <a class="link" href={deckPath}>Download slides (PDF)</a>
          </div>
        </object>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
